// Title: Rundll32 Execution Without Parameters
// Sigma ID: 5bb68627-3198-40ca-b458-49f973db8752
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Bartlomiej Czyz, Relativity
// Date: 2021-01-31 | Modified: 2023-02-28
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, T1021.002, T1570, execution, T1569.002
// Description: Detects rundll32 execution without parameters as observed when running Metasploit
//   windows/smb/psexec exploit module
// False positives:
//   - False positives may occur if a user called rundll32 from CLI with no options
// References:
//   - https://bczyz1.github.io/2021/01/30/psexec.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_without_parameters.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine in~ ("rundll32.exe", "rundll32")
